Requirements: 30   with obligations: 29   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Every requirement of a mandate is accounted for on its own, and an obligation
    quotes the requirement it came from. The mandate's opening summary is accounted for
    last, against the obligations the rest of the mandate already produced, so that a
    property the rest of the mandate states does not become a second obligation and a
    property only the summary states is not lost.
    -> account-each-requirement-on-its-own  [functional/explicit]
       Every requirement of a mandate is accounted for on its own, and an obligation
       quotes the requirement it came from.
    -> opening-summary-accounted-for-last  [functional/explicit]
       The mandate's opening summary is accounted for last, against the obligations the
       rest of the mandate already produced, so that a property the rest of the mandate
       states does not become a second obligation and a property only the summary states
       is not lost.

[constraint-01] A requirement other than the opening summary is accounted for by a step
    asked about that requirement alone, and that step returns exactly one account of it.
    -> single-account-per-requirement-step  [functional/explicit]
       A requirement other than the opening summary is accounted for by a step asked
       about that requirement alone, and that step returns exactly one account of it.

[constraint-02] The quotation an obligation carries is chosen from the text of the
    requirement its step was asked about, so a quotation belonging to a different
    requirement cannot be given.
    -> quotation-from-asked-requirement  [invariant/explicit]
       The quotation an obligation carries is chosen from the text of the requirement
       its step was asked about, so a quotation belonging to a different requirement
       cannot be given.

[constraint-03] No step that accounts for a requirement other than the opening summary
    is asked to account for the opening summary.
    -> no-summary-cross-accounting  [invariant/explicit]
       No step that accounts for a requirement other than the opening summary is asked
       to account for the opening summary.

[constraint-04] The opening summary is accounted for by a step that first divides it
    into stretches of its own words and then decides, for each stretch, whether the
    obligations already derived from the rest of the mandate require the same thing.
    -> summary-divided-into-stretches-and-compared  [functional/explicit]
       The opening summary is accounted for by a step that first divides it into
       stretches of its own words and then decides, for each stretch, whether the
       obligations already derived from the rest of the mandate require the same thing.

[constraint-05] Every stretch is a substring of the opening summary, and every stretch
    is decided exactly once.
    -> summary-stretches-are-substrings-and-decided-once  [invariant/explicit]
       Every stretch is a substring of the opening summary, and every stretch is decided
       exactly once.

[constraint-06] A stretch the already-derived obligations require yields no obligation.
    -> already-required-stretches-yield-no-obligation  [invariant/explicit]
       A stretch the already-derived obligations require yields no obligation.

[constraint-07] A stretch they do not require yields obligations, derived by a step
    asked about that stretch alone.
    -> new-stretches-yield-obligations-from-stretch-alone  [functional/explicit]
       A stretch they do not require yields obligations, derived by a step asked about
       that stretch alone.

[constraint-08] The step that decides whether a stretch is already required yields no
    obligations itself.
    -> cannot-accounting-step-yields-no-obligations  [invariant/explicit]
       The step that decides whether a stretch is already required yields no obligations
       itself.

[constraint-09] An obligation derived from a stretch carries that stretch as its
    quotation, taken from the mandate rather than from the answer that named it.
    -> stretch-quotation-from-mandate  [invariant/explicit]
       An obligation derived from a stretch carries that stretch as its quotation, taken
       from the mandate rather than from the answer that named it.

[constraint-10] A step may name the model it runs on; a step that names none uses the
    run's own model.
    -> step-may-name-own-model  [functional/explicit]
       A step may name the model it runs on; a step that names none uses the run's own
       model.

[constraint-11] A completed run says which model each step used.
    -> completed-run-records-step-models  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       A completed run says which model each step used.

[constraint-12] Where a step tells the answering party what order its request presents
    its parts in, that statement is true of the request as sent.
    -> request-order-statement-matches-sent-request  [invariant/explicit]
       Where a step tells the answering party what order its request presents its parts
       in, that statement is true of the request as sent.

[exclusion-01] Which text in the mandate counts as a requirement, and how many
    requirements are found.
    -> does-not-determine-requirement-count-or-scope  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not alter which text in the mandate counts as a requirement, or
       how many requirements are found.

[exclusion-02] Whether the obligations derived for a requirement are the right ones for
    it.
    -> does-not-change-obligation-selection-correctness  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not alter whether the obligations derived for a requirement are
       the right ones for it.

[exclusion-03] What the review does with an answer it cannot read at all.
    -> does-not-stop-review-on-unreadable-answer  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not alter what the review does with an answer it cannot read at
       all.

[exclusion-04] Combining obligations that state the same thing as one another.
    -> combine-agreeing-accounts-2  [functional/explicit]
       The review combines agreeing accounts of the same requirement into one account
       and carries on.

[exclusion-05] Which model is the right one for any step, and what any step costs.
    -> step-model-selection-and-cost-unchanged  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not alter which model is the right one for any step or what any
       step costs.

[exclusion-06] Comparing figures recorded before this change with figures recorded after
    it.
    -> no-before-after-figure-comparison  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not compare figures recorded before this change with figures
       recorded after it.

